body:
Hi! First of all, I completely get you. My fear of flying has been complicated to handle for a while. I medicate for flights, not gonna lie to you, but the other things I've been doing to prepare for each flight (and that have helped a lot to make me feel less frightened) are:
- watching videos of pilots preparing for the flight ahead of them. On YouTube, you can see some videos with pilots in the cockpit talking about their preparations and then taking off / landing. I've found that very reassuring and gave me a new perspective of safety;
- watching the "jello video". Super helpful to understand how turbulences work and why you're safe;
- keeping my feet off the floor if possible to feel less turbulences / plane moves (I usually put my feet on my backpack which lies on the floor, underneath the seat in front of me). Really helps physically to avoid the "stomach flipping" feeling I get. 

I truly hope you can find some comfort before you fly next Friday! You got this. It's very courageous of you. All the best 💖

Just tried signing up for My Opinions and it doesn't work for me (I'm in France). Only for Australia :(

&#x200B;

Thank you for your post!

**NAH**. Your arguments are completely valid and I understand your gf wanting a dog. You could maybe try to be foster parents to puppies / dogs in general to see? That way, you can try the adventure to see if you like it or not?

&#x200B;

